E4  Kaluza-Klein isometry: Z1(flat aleph, lambda = 1/(n+1), cH = 2 cV)  ~  SL(n+1,R)/SO(p',q')
  n=2: tr((M^-1 dM)^2) == G_(1/(n+1))(dy,dy) + 2 y(dx,dx) with det M = 1: True
  n=3: tr((M^-1 dM)^2) == G_(1/(n+1))(dy,dy) + 2 y(dx,dx) with det M = 1: True
  n=4: tr((M^-1 dM)^2) == G_(1/(n+1))(dy,dy) + 2 y(dx,dx) with det M = 1: True
  dim SL(n+1)/SO = n(n+3)/2 = dim Y; Einstein constant of tr((M^-1 dM)^2) on SL(n+1)/SO is -(n+1)/4 (Prop. F1 at n+1)

